<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">American Popular Revolutionary Alliance</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1924">1924</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as APRA, Peruvian Aprista Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The American Popular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tongmenghui">Revolutionary Alliance</a> (APRA) is a Peruvian political party founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-raul-haya-de-la-torre">Víctor Raúl Haya de la Torre</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1924 as an anti-imperialist movement for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America</a>, and organised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> in 1930. Peru's first mass party, it was repeatedly banned and fought bloody conflicts with the army, including the Trujillo uprising of 1932. It finally won the presidency under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alan-garcia">Alan García</a> in 1985 and again in 2006.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/american-popular-revolutionary-alliance.jpg" alt="American Popular Revolutionary Alliance" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alianza Popular Revolucionaria Americana · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:APRA_Peru_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
